# Cache-Control rules.
#
# Read by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. GitHub Pages IGNORES this file — it
# serves everything with a fixed 10-minute cache and cannot be configured,
# so Lighthouse's "Use efficient cache lifetimes" audit is unfixable there.
#
# Zola fingerprints CSS, JS and the banner with ?h=<hash>, so a new hash is
# requested the moment the file changes. That makes immutable caching safe.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Not fingerprinted — rename the file if you ever need to bust these.
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
